RESULT: 27/27 checks passed in 1.9s
VERDICT: Codex's xi = (b - a gamma)/d is 2(b - a gamma)/V_spin -- a ruler projection over the SHEET observable.  The deck
  sends xi -> -xi and fixes every base-field invariant: PINCH-1's two null limits are deck partners and the live seat nu*
  is the deck-fixed continuation.  Only a Kummer coordinate can resolve the pinch, because the branch locus is TANGENT to
  the horizon there (not transverse), so contact order governs the readout and the resolution is a weighted (1,2) blow-up
  with xi the coordinate on its exceptional divisor.  No realisable loop encircles the pinch; the deck glues the ends.
